cond-quarter earnings, and the pain quickly spread to the other FAANG stocks—Apple, Amazon, Netflix, and Alphabet—which have also dropped since then. The Invesco QQQ ETF (QQQ), which tracks the 100 largest nonfinancial companies listed on Nasdaq, has also declined 4.2% from its its peak price of $182.82 through yesterday’s close.", "external_links": ["https://www.tumblr.com/widgets/share/tool?posttype=link&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.barrons.com%2Farticles%2Flive-by-the-fang-stocks-die-with-the-fang-stocks-1533064218%3Fmod%3Dyahoobarrons%26ru%3Dyahoo%26yptr%3Dyahoo%26soc_src%3Dsocial-sh%26soc_trk%3Dtu&content=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.barrons.com%2Farticles%2Flive-by-the-fang-stocks-die-with-the-fang-stocks-1533064218%3Fmod%3Dyahoobarrons%26ru%3Dyahoo%26yptr%3Dyahoo%26soc_src%3Dsocial-sh%26soc_trk%3Dtu&caption=If%20you%20live%20by%20the%20FAANGs%2C%20you%20die%20by%2"], "published": "2018-07-31T22:39:00.000+03:00", "crawled": "2018-08-01T01:51:05.000+03:00", "highlightTitle": ""}